    <div class="container">

        <h1>Database & SQL 📚</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
            Basic database and SQL study materials.
        </p>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>1. What is a Database?</h2>

            <p>
                A database is an organized collection of data
                that can be stored, managed and accessed easily.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>2. DBMS</h2>

            <p>
                DBMS stands for Database Management System.
                It is software used to create, store and manage data.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>3. SQL</h2>

            <p>
                SQL stands for Structured Query Language.
                It is used to communicate with relational databases.
            </p>

            <p>
                Example:
                <code>SELECT * FROM students;</code>
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>4. Primary Key</h2>

            <p>
                A primary key uniquely identifies each record
                in a database table.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>5. CRUD Operations</h2>

            <p>
                CRUD stands for Create, Read, Update and Delete.
                These are the basic operations performed on data.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>

